unit: REVIEW-build-daemon-fabric-standalone
commits: c1cd6e217 (the standalone construction)
what: Fabric is a standalone object the daemon holds across stop. `FabricPart::new`
  (sovereign-mesh/src/fabric.rs) assembles the part from its seed, mesh, mesh_store
  and app_registry; `AppState::new_with_fabric_and_serving_and_node`
  (sovereign-daemon/src/state.rs) takes the built Arc, while the seed-shaped
  constructor builds one and delegates so the rail harness and test call sites are
  unchanged. `EmbeddedDaemon` holds the Arc in a new `fabric` field, set by
  `start_daemon` before `AppState` and kept across `stop_inner` (cleared on Leave),
  exposed by `EmbeddedDaemon::fabric()`. Every `app_state.inner.fabric` read is
  unchanged. Behaviour-preserving.
corrections (PROMPT §6, ralph/DECISIONS.md 2026-09-18): the row's "then move
  known_meshes/forget_mesh/switch_mesh/try_resume/resume_active and the running-side
  create_mesh/join_mesh/leave/rotate_invite/current_invite onto Fabric" half is
  re-scoped out. Those methods are daemon assembly (DC §4.1 reserves
  start_daemon/stop_inner/shutdown) and Fabric lives in sovereign-mesh, which cannot
  name the daemon ([[forbid]] sovereign-mesh -> sovereign-daemon). Reproduced:
  try_resume -> resume_active -> start_daemon; switch_mesh -> stop_inner + resume_active;
  create_mesh_with/join_mesh -> start_daemon; leave -> stop_inner; current_invite reads
  the running DaemonState; rotate_invite requires app_state. The pure membership state
  already moved at 8a8936b87.
checks: CLEAN exit=0 (debug target 39G, under 50G); LINT exit=0 (5 crates,
  --all-targets, errors 0); LAYER exit=0 ("every edge points down or sideways,
  fan-in within caps"); TEST(sovereign-mesh) exit=0 (613 pass);
  TEST(sovereign-daemon) exit=0 (706 pass).
